IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa10-types`

-- coa10-default.l4: Chapter 10, ss 451 to 453 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom): the offence, the court order and
-- the civil penalty for default in filing accounts and reports. Lines 6123-6144 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE = the text says the case is
-- within the rule; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the words>"`); NOTHING = the text does not decide
-- (each such branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The pounds a level on the standard scale stands for are not in the Act: INPUTS, never guessed.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 451: default in filing accounts and reports: offences
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 451(1): every person who immediately before the end of the period was a director commits an offence if the
-- requirements of s 441 are not complied with before the end of the period for filing. The "complied with" answer is
-- coa10-filing's `s 441(1) the requirements were complied with before the end of the period for filing`, taken as an input.
-- src:6125 | (1) If the requirements of section 441 (duty to file accounts and reports) are not complied with in relation to a company's accounts and reports for a financial year before the end of the period for filing those accounts and reports, every person who immediately before the end of that period was a director of the company commits an offence.
@ref s 451(1) Every director commits an offence if the accounts and reports are not filed in time (src:6125)
GIVEN `s 441(1) the requirements were complied with before the end of the period for filing` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 451(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 441(1) the requirements were complied with before the end of the period for filing`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "If" not met): "If the requirements of section 441 (duty to file accounts and reports) are not complied with ... before the end of the period for filing"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        IF `the person was a director of the company immediately before the end of the period for filing`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every person who immediately before the end of that period was a director of the company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the requirements were complied with is not known

-- s 451(2): "It is a defence ... to prove that ...": when it is not proved the answer is JUST FALSE for this provision's defence,
-- worded "this section gives no defence on these facts" (ruling of 2026-11-05), never "no defence at all".
-- src:6126 | (2) It is a defence for a person charged with such an offence to prove that he took all reasonable steps for securing that those requirements would be complied with before the end of that period.
@ref s 451(2) It is a defence to prove that all reasonable steps were taken (src:6126)
GIVEN `the person proves that he took all reasonable steps for securing that those requirements would be complied with before the end of that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 451(2) this section gives the person a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF `the person proves that he took all reasonable steps for securing that those requirements would be complied with before the end of that period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (ruling of 2026-11-05, a defence not proved): "It is a defence for a person charged with such an offence to prove that he took all reasonable steps for securing that those requirements would be complied with before the end of that period"

-- src:6127 | (3) It is not a defence to prove that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part.
@ref s 451(3) It is not a defence to prove that the documents were not prepared (src:6127)
GIVEN `the person proves that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 451(3) proving that the documents were not prepared as required is a defence to the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person proves that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is not a defence to prove that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of proving that the documents were not prepared

-- "A person guilty of an offence under this section" (s 451(4)): the offence is committed and the defence does not succeed.
-- src:6125 | (1) If the requirements of section 441 (duty to file accounts and reports) are not complied with in relation to a company's accounts and reports for a financial year before the end of the period for filing those accounts and reports, every person who immediately before the end of that period was a director of the company commits an offence.
-- src:6126 | (2) It is a defence for a person charged with such an offence to prove that he took all reasonable steps for securing that those requirements would be complied with before the end of that period.
-- src:6127 | (3) It is not a defence to prove that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part.
@ref s 451(1), (2) Guilt: the offence committed and no defence made out (src:6125-6127)
GIVEN `s 451(1) the person commits an offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 451(2) this section gives the person a defence on these facts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 451(4) the person is guilty of an offence under section 451` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 451(1) the person commits an offence`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): no offence under s 451(1) is committed, so no person is guilty of one
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 451(2) this section gives the person a defence on these facts`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence for a person charged with such an offence to prove that he took all reasonable steps"
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the defence is made out is not known
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is committed is not known

-- s 451(4): the penalty. The file prints two daily default fines run together on line 6128 (the first text: one-tenth of
-- level 5; the second: one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4). The core's `Penalty` has no constructor for the
-- second, so the second text has a record of its own (NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- src:6128 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 451(4) First text: summary conviction, a fine not exceeding level 5 and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 5 (src:6128)
`s 451(4) the penalty in the first text` MEANS
    Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, (JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)), (JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1)), FALSE

DECLARE `s 451 daily default fine limit` IS ONE OF
    `s 451 one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale`
    `s 451 one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale`

DECLARE `s 451 the penalty in the second text` HAS
    `s 451 how convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
    `s 451 the fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale` IS A `Fine limit`
    `s 451 the daily default fine for continued contravention` IS A `s 451 daily default fine limit`

-- src:6128 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 451(4) Second text: summary conviction, a fine not exceeding level 5 and a daily default fine of one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 (src:6128)
`s 451(4) the penalty in the second text` MEANS
    `s 451 the penalty in the second text` OF `on summary conviction`, `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1, `s 451 one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale`

-- In pounds, from the amounts of levels 4 and 5 on the standard scale (not in the Act: inputs).
-- src:6128 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 451(4) The fine on summary conviction, in pounds (src:6128)
GIVEN `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 451(4) the greatest fine on summary conviction in pounds` MEANS
    `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale (in pounds)`

-- src:6128 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 451(4) The daily default fine for continued contravention, in pounds (src:6128)
GIVEN `the text relied on` IS A `s 441 text of the sections the file prints twice`
      `the amount of level 4 on the standard scale (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 451(4) the greatest daily default fine in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the text relied on`
    WHEN `s 441 first text in the file` THEN `the amount of level 5 on the standard scale (in pounds)` DIVIDED BY 10
    WHEN `s 441 second text in the file` THEN (max 5000 `the amount of level 4 on the standard scale (in pounds)`) DIVIDED BY 10

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 452: default in filing accounts and reports: court order
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "within 14 days after the service of a notice": the last day is the service day plus 14. Made good after that, or still not
-- made good after that day: the directors failed. Made good on or before it: they did not fail (a period fixed in the text's
-- own words, outside it the answer is JUST FALSE). Not made good and the 14 days still running: not yet decided.
-- src:6132 | (b) the directors of the company fail to make good the default within 14 days after the service of a notice on them requiring compliance,
@ref s 452(1)(b) The directors fail to make good the default within 14 days after the service of a notice (src:6132)
GIVEN `the date on which the notice requiring compliance was served on the directors` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the default was made good (if it has been)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 452(1)(b) the directors failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice` MEANS
    LET `the last day` MEANS `the date on which the notice requiring compliance was served on the directors` PLUS 14
    IN CONSIDER `the date on which the default was made good (if it has been)`
       WHEN JUST made THEN
           IF made AT MOST `the last day`
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a period fixed in the text's own words, ruling of 2026-11-05): "fail to make good the default within 14 days after the service of a notice on them requiring compliance"
           ELSE JUST TRUE
       WHEN NOTHING THEN
           IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the last day`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 14 days are still running and the default has not been made good

-- src:6130 | (1) If—
-- src:6131 | (a) the requirements of section 441 (duty to file accounts and reports) are not complied with in relation to a company's accounts and reports for a financial year before the end of the period for filing those accounts and reports, and
-- src:6132 | (b) the directors of the company fail to make good the default within 14 days after the service of a notice on them requiring compliance,
-- src:6133 | the court may, on the application of any member or creditor of the company or of the registrar, make an order directing the directors (or any of them) to make good the default within such time as may be specified in the order.
@ref s 452(1) The court may order the directors to make good the default (src:6130-6133)
GIVEN `s 441(1) the requirements were complied with before the end of the period for filing` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 452(1)(b) the directors failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a member or creditor of the company or the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 452(1) the court may order the directors to make good the default` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 441(1) the requirements were complied with before the end of the period for filing`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the requirements of section 441 (duty to file accounts and reports) are not complied with in relation to a company's accounts and reports for a financial year before the end of the period for filing"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 452(1)(b) the directors failed to make good the default within 14 days after the service of the notice`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the directors of the company fail to make good the default within 14 days after the service of a notice on them requiring compliance"
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
            IF `the applicant is a member or creditor of the company or the registrar`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the application of any member or creditor of the company or of the registrar"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the 14 days are still running
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the requirements were complied with is not known

-- src:6134 | (2) The court's order may provide that all costs (in Scotland, expenses) of and incidental to the application are to be borne by the directors.
@ref s 452(2) The court's order may provide that the costs are borne by the directors (src:6134)
GIVEN `the court makes an order under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 452(2) the court's order may provide that all the costs are borne by the directors` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court's order may provide"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 453: civil penalty for failure to file accounts and reports
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6136 | (1) Where the requirements of section 441 are not complied with in relation to a company's accounts and reports for a financial year before the end of the period for filing those accounts and reports, the company is liable to a civil penalty.
@ref s 453(1) The company is liable to a civil penalty (src:6136)
GIVEN `s 441(1) the requirements were complied with before the end of the period for filing` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 453(1) the company is liable to a civil penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 441(1) the requirements were complied with before the end of the period for filing`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a "where" not met, ruling of 2026-11-05): "Where the requirements of section 441 are not complied with in relation to a company's accounts and reports for a financial year before the end of the period for filing those accounts and reports, the company is liable to a civil penalty"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the requirements were complied with is not known

-- src:6137 | This is in addition to any liability of the directors under section 451.
@ref s 453(1) The civil penalty is in addition to the directors' liability under section 451 (src:6137)
GIVEN `the directors are liable under section 451` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 453(1) the company's liability is in addition to the directors' liability under section 451` MEANS
    IF `the directors are liable under section 451`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This is in addition to any liability of the directors under section 451"

-- (2)(a): the length of the period between the end of the period for filing and the day on which the requirements are complied with.
-- src:6138 | (2) The amount of the penalty shall be determined in accordance with regulations made by the Secretary of State by reference to—
-- src:6139 | (a) the length of the period between the end of the period for filing the accounts and reports in question and the day on which the requirements are complied with, and
@ref s 453(2)(a) The length of the period between the end of the period for filing and compliance (src:6138-6139)
GIVEN `the day on which the period for filing ends` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the requirements are complied with` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 453(2)(a) the number of days between the end of the period for filing and the day on which the requirements are complied with` MEANS
    (Day `the day on which the requirements are complied with`) MINUS (Day `the day on which the period for filing ends`)

-- (2): the amount is "determined in accordance with regulations made by the Secretary of State": not in the sources, so an input.
-- src:6138 | (2) The amount of the penalty shall be determined in accordance with regulations made by the Secretary of State by reference to—
-- src:6139 | (a) the length of the period between the end of the period for filing the accounts and reports in question and the day on which the requirements are complied with, and
-- src:6140 | (b) whether the company is a private or public company.
@ref s 453(2) The amount of the penalty is fixed by regulations (src:6138-6140)
GIVEN `s 453(1) the company is liable to a civil penalty` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the amount the regulations fix for a company of this kind that complied this many days late (in pounds)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 453(2) the amount of the civil penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 453(1) the company is liable to a civil penalty`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST `the amount the regulations fix for a company of this kind that complied this many days late (in pounds)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the company is liable to a penalty only where s 453(1) is met
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is liable is not known

-- src:6141 | (3) The penalty may be recovered by the registrar and is to be paid into the Consolidated Fund.
@ref s 453(3) The registrar may recover the penalty, and it is paid into the Consolidated Fund (src:6141)
GIVEN `s 453(1) the company is liable to a civil penalty` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 453(3) the registrar may recover the penalty from the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 453(1) the company is liable to a civil penalty`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The penalty may be recovered by the registrar"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is liable is not known

-- src:6141 | (3) The penalty may be recovered by the registrar and is to be paid into the Consolidated Fund.
@ref s 453(3) The penalty is to be paid into the Consolidated Fund (src:6141)
GIVEN `s 453(1) the company is liable to a civil penalty` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 453(3) the penalty is to be paid into the Consolidated Fund` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 453(1) the company is liable to a civil penalty`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the penalty ... is to be paid into the Consolidated Fund"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is liable is not known

-- src:6142 | (4) It is not a defence in proceedings under this section to prove that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part.
@ref s 453(4) It is not a defence to prove that the documents were not prepared (src:6142)
GIVEN `the company proves that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 453(4) proving that the documents were not prepared as required is a defence to the civil penalty` MEANS
    IF `the company proves that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is not a defence in proceedings under this section to prove that the documents in question were not in fact prepared as required by this Part."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of proving that the documents were not prepared
